ホロライブの清楚担当、みんなのアイドルの夏色まつりです！
I'm hololive's purity representative, everyone's idol, Natsuiro Matsuri!

6
00:01:58,200 --> 00:02:01,800
今日はMC、お願いします。頑張りまーす！
I'm your host today. I'll do my best!

7
00:02:02,500 --> 00:02:08,500
じゃあ、今日参加してくださる人たち一人ずつ行きますよ。
Now then, let's go one by one with today's participants.

8
00:02:08,500 --> 00:02:11,500
じゃあヨピピからお願いします！
Yopipi, please go first!

9
00:02:11,800 --> 00:02:16,800
はい！イオフォリア、オビサ！どうもです！ホロライブインドネシアからイオフィです！
Yes! Ioforia, obisa! Hello, I'm Iofi from hololive Indonesia!

10
00:02:17,000 --> 00:02:21,000
今日はオノマトペを、ちょっと...
Today, about onomatopoeia... a little...

11
00:02:21,000 --> 00:02:22,500
可愛い。
Cute.

12
00:02:22,500 --> 00:02:26,000
のことちょっと、勉強したいと思います！よろしくお願いします！
I'd like to study about that today! Nice to meet you!

13
00:02:26,000 --> 00:02:27,500
お願いしまーす！
Nice to have you!

14
00:02:27,500 --> 00:02:29,500
じゃあ、こぼちゃん！
Next up, Kobo-chan!

15
00:02:30,000 --> 00:02:35,000
ワカワカワカ... Kobo Kanaeru at your service! Let me be your sun to shine your day, ahem!
Waka waka waka... Kobo Kanaeru at your service! Let me be your sun to shine your day, ahem!

16
00:02:35,000 --> 00:02:38,200
コボ・カナエル、レイン・シャーマンです！
I'm Kobo Kanaeru, the rain shaman!

17
00:02:38,200 --> 00:02:44,200
今日はオノマトペア、勝ちだ！お願いします！
Today, for onomatopoeia... ah, I'll win! Please take care of me!

18
00:02:44,200 --> 00:02:50,000
頑張ろう！
Let's do this!

19
00:02:50,000 --> 00:02:52,500
じゃあ、続いてジジ！
All right, next up is Gigi!

20
00:02:52,500 --> 00:02:57,000
こんばんは！ジジです！ちむにん...
Good evening! I'm Gigi! A chimeranian...

21
00:02:57,000 --> 00:03:02,000
えーっと、日本語ちょっと、上手じゃない。
Um, my Japanese is a bit... not that good.

22
00:03:02,000 --> 00:03:07,500
オノマトペ、ちょっと、日本語を頑張って！
Onomatopoeia... I'll do my best with Japanese!

23
00:03:07,500 --> 00:03:09,000
頑張ります！
I'll do my best!

24
00:03:09,000 --> 00:03:13,500
ありがとー！頑張れー！
Thank you! Do your best!

25
00:03:13,500 --> 00:03:17,500
はい！じゃあ続いて、ほぼJPのベっちゃん！
All right! Next is Bae-chan, who's basically JP!

26
00:03:17,500 --> 00:03:21,000
いやいや、What's up? 我らはChaos！ホロライブのハコス・ベールズです！
No no no. What's up? We are Chaos! I'm Hakos Baelz from hololive!

27
00:03:21,000 --> 00:03:25,200
今日は翻訳担当でやりたいと思います！よろしくお願いしまーす！
Today, I'll be handling the translations! Looking forward to working with you!

28
00:03:25,200 --> 00:03:27,200
お願いしまーす！
Looking forward to it!

29
00:03:29,500 --> 00:03:32,000
はい、じゃあ最後、ラオラー！
Yes! And finally, Raora!

30
00:03:32,500 --> 00:03:37,000
あ、こんにちはー！ラオラ・パンテーラです！
Ah, hello! I'm Raora Panthera!

31
00:03:37,000 --> 00:03:45,500
今日は、絵を描いたり、日本語で話したり、頑張りまっそう！
Today, I'll draw pictures, speak in Japanese, and do my best!

32
00:03:45,500 --> 00:03:51,500
はーい、お願いしまーす！
Yes, let's do this!

33
00:03:51,500 --> 00:03:57,000
はい！ということでね、本日はですね、皆さんにオノマトペクイズに答えてもらいます！
All right! So today, everyone will be answering an onomatopoeia quiz!

34
00:03:57,000 --> 00:04:03,200
ちょっとね、日本独特の表現とかもたくさんあるんですが、頑張って答えてね。
There are plenty of expressions unique to Japan, but give it your best shot!

35
00:04:06,000 --> 00:04:11,500
ぜひね、日本に来る際はいっぱい使っていただきたいなと思います！
Whenever you visit Japan, I really hope you'll get to use them a lot!

36
00:04:12,000 --> 00:04:17,500
はい、ということで！早速第1問いきましょう！
All right, without further ado, let's move on to Question 1!

37
00:04:19,500 --> 00:04:22,000
Question one!

38
00:04:22,000 --> 00:04:24,000
First question!

39
00:04:24,000 --> 00:04:28,500
このオノマトペは何を表しているでしょうか？
What does this onomatopoeia represent?

40
00:04:28,500 --> 00:04:31,000
「コケコッコー」
\"Cock-a-doodle-doo\" [Kokekokko].

41
00:04:32,000 --> 00:04:38,000
What's this? What's the sound of... / コケコッコー。
What's this? What's the sound of... / Kokekokko.

42
00:04:39,000 --> 00:04:46,000
Where do you hear this onomatopoeia from? Onomatopoeia... / Poeeea?

43
00:04:46,000 --> 00:04:48,800
ああ、わからない！
Ah, I have no idea!

44
00:04:48,800 --> 00:04:51,500
わからない場合どうします？
What do we do if we don't know?

45
00:04:51,500 --> 00:04:57,000
あ、じゃあヒントは、動物の鳴き声ですね！何の動物の鳴き声でしょうか？
Well, the hint is: it's an animal call! What kind of animal call is it?

46
00:04:57,000 --> 00:05:00,000
It's an animal cry! What animal makes...

47
00:05:00,008 --> 00:10:00,016
Error processing subtitles for this segment.

48
00:10:00,216 --> 00:10:01,016
キメラ？
A chimera?

49
00:10:01,016 --> 00:10:01,816
Oh my god.

50
00:10:01,816 --> 00:10:03,316
キマイラ言うのやめて？
Stop calling it a chimera.

51
00:10:03,416 --> 00:10:06,716
ほいじゃあ、ちょっと一人ずつまた聞いていきますか？
Alright then, shall we ask everyone one by one again?

52
00:10:06,716 --> 00:10:08,516
かわいい、みんな。
Everyone's is so cute.

53
00:10:09,316 --> 00:10:11,716
えー、じゃあ、よぴぴ。
Okay, first up, Yopipi.

54
00:10:11,916 --> 00:10:14,616
はい！カエルです！Frogです！
Yes! It's a frog! A frog!

55
00:10:14,916 --> 00:10:18,016
あー！Frog！ケロ、ケロケロでしょ？
Ah! Frog! Ribbit, it goes "kero kero", right?

56
00:10:18,016 --> 00:10:19,416
なるほど。
I see.

57
00:10:19,416 --> 00:10:20,616
カエルね！
はい！はい！
A frog, then!
Yes! Yes!

58
00:10:20,716 --> 00:10:22,816
じゃあ、続いてこぼちゃん。
Alright, next up, Kobo-chan.

59
00:10:23,216 --> 00:10:27,216
あたしも、かえ...カエル？カエル、Frog！
Me too... a fr... frog? Frog, frog!

60
00:10:26,516 --> 00:10:29,016
Frog！カエル！はい、ケロケロ。
Frog! A frog! Yes, ribbit ribbit.

61
00:10:29,016 --> 00:10:32,416
漢字で書いてる！すごーい！
She wrote it in kanji! Amazing!

62
00:10:33,416 --> 00:10:36,516
まつりも書けないよ、蛙。
Even Matsuri can't write that kanji for frog.

63
00:10:37,316 --> 00:10:39,416
はい、じゃあ続いてジジ！
Alright, next up, Gigi!

64
00:10:39,516 --> 00:10:42,516
はい！ケロケロ！けろっぴ！
Yes! Kero kero! Keroppi!

65
00:10:42,516 --> 00:10:46,016
あ、けろけろけろっぴ！おー！なるほどー！
Ah, Kero Kero Keroppi! Oh, I see!

66
00:10:46,516 --> 00:10:48,316
じゃあ、べーちゃん！
Alright, Bae-chan!

67
00:10:48,516 --> 00:10:50,016
あ、カエルです！
Ah, it's a frog!

68
00:10:49,816 --> 00:10:51,516
お？カエルかな？
カエルです！
Oh? Is that a frog?
It's a frog!

69
00:10:52,016 --> 00:10:53,316
カエル？
A frog?

70
00:10:53,316 --> 00:10:55,216
カエル！
Frog!

71
00:10:55,216 --> 00:10:57,616
カエル...一瞬ちょっとね...
A frog... for a second...

72
00:10:57,616 --> 00:10:59,816
一瞬ネズミに見えたんだけどね。
it kind of looked like a rat for a moment, though.

73
00:10:59,816 --> 00:11:04,216
いや、ちょっと...さすがにね、カエル見たことないんで...
Well, lately... I haven't seen a frog, so...

74
00:11:04,416 --> 00:11:07,416
一応カエル。画伯だ。
A frog, supposedly. A true artist.

75
00:11:07,416 --> 00:11:10,516
その隣の、えーラオラ！めっちゃ絵上手い！
And next to her, Raora! Your drawing is so good!

76
00:11:10,816 --> 00:11:12,716
かわいい！
Cute!

77
00:11:12,716 --> 00:11:14,316
Yay!

78
00:11:14,516 --> 00:11:17,016
はい、カエルですね？
Alright, so that's a frog, right?

79
00:11:17,316 --> 00:11:19,516
うん！カエルです！
Yep! It's a frog!

80
00:11:19,816 --> 00:11:23,016
はい！じゃあ「ケロケロ」、正解は...
Yes! Then for "kero kero", the correct answer is...

81
00:11:23,016 --> 00:11:26,516
「カエル」でございます！
...a frog!

82
00:11:26,516 --> 00:11:29,016
イェーイ！正解！やったー！
Yay! Correct! Hurray!

83
00:11:29,016 --> 00:11:30,416
Nice, nice, yeah!

84
00:11:30,416 --> 00:11:32,016
Easy! Easy! Easy!

85
00:11:32,016 --> 00:11:34,516
やったー！簡単だった！
Hurray! That was so easy!

86
00:11:34,816 --> 00:11:36,016
日本語上手！
Good Japanese!

87
00:11:36,016 --> 00:11:37,416
日本語上手よ！
Your Japanese is so good!

88
00:11:37,416 --> 00:11:39,016
ねー！
Yeah!

89
00:11:39,116 --> 00:11:41,516
じゃ、続いて行きますよ。
Alright, moving on to the next one.

90
00:11:41,516 --> 00:11:43,816
続いては、えー、こちら！
Next up is... this!

91
00:11:44,216 --> 00:11:48,016
馬の鳴き声は？日本だと何と言うでしょう？
"What sound does a horse make?" What do they say in Japan?

92
00:11:48,016 --> 00:11:50,516
What sound does a horse make?

93
00:11:50,516 --> 00:11:51,816
馬ね。
A horse.

94
00:11:52,016 --> 00:11:54,016
Japanese onomatopoeia.

95
00:11:55,516 --> 00:11:57,516
分からなーい！
I don't know!

96
00:11:57,516 --> 00:11:58,516
何て言うの？
What do they say?

97
00:11:58,516 --> 00:12:02,016
何て聞こえるかな？何て聞こえるかなー？
How does it sound to you? What does it sound like?

98
00:12:04,516 --> 00:12:07,516
うーん...
Hmm...

99
00:12:08,516 --> 00:12:10,516
Mimi...

100
00:12:10,716 --> 00:12:13,516
イメージ、イメージして？
Imagine, just picture it?

101
00:12:15,516 --> 00:12:18,516
That's right Gigi, feel it from the heart!

102
00:12:18,516 --> 00:12:20,016
Feel it!

103
00:12:20,016 --> 00:12:21,016
You can do it!

104
00:12:20,516 --> 00:12:23,516
一人ずつ鳴いてもらうからね？
I'm going to have each of you make the sound, okay?

105
00:12:24,016 --> 00:12:27,516
She's gonna ask each of you to sound out the...

106
00:12:27,516 --> 00:12:31,516
...onomatopoeia that you have come up with.

107
00:12:35,016 --> 00:12:37,516
オッケー？オッケー、オッケー？
Ready? Ready, okay?

108
00:12:37,716 --> 00:12:40,016
全然知らん？
You have no idea?

109
00:12:40,516 --> 00:12:43,816
じゃあ一人ずつ鳴いてもらいますか？
Then should we have everyone make the sound one by one?

110
00:12:44,016 --> 00:12:47,816
じゃ、よぴぴから。よぴぴの馬の鳴き声...
Alright, starting with Yopipi. Yopipi's horse sound...

111
00:12:47,816 --> 00:12:49,516
お願いします。ボイス！
...please. Voice!

112
00:12:49,516 --> 00:12:52,516
「はりきっていこう！」です！
It's "Let's give it our all!"

113
00:12:52,516 --> 00:12:55,316
はりきっていこう？！それ？！それ違くない？！
"Let's give it our all"?! That?! Isn't that wrong?!

114
00:12:55,716 --> 00:12:57,316
I don't think...

115
00:12:57,316 --> 00:12:58,516
そうやって鳴く？！
Does it make that sound?!

116
00:12:58,516 --> 00:13:01,016
馬これしかないですよ！
Horses only do this!

117
00:13:00,016 --> 00:13:02,016
ウマ娘すぎる！
That's way too Uma Musume!

118
00:13:02,016 --> 00:13:05,516
馬これしか知らないですよ、馬！
That's the only horse I know!

119
00:13:05,816 --> 00:13:08,516
じゃあ、続いて、えー、こぼちゃん！
Alright, next up, Kobo-chan!

120
00:13:09,516 --> 00:13:13,016
あー、「ひーほー！ひーほー！」
Ah, "Hee-haw! Hee-haw!"

121
00:13:13,016 --> 00:13:15,516
あー！ひーふー？ひーふー？
Ah! Hee-hoo? Hee-hoo?

122
00:13:15,516 --> 00:13:17,016
ひーふー！
Hee-hoo!

123
00:13:17,016 --> 00:13:19,016
I feel like that's a different sound.

124
00:13:19,016 --> 00:13:21,016
ロバじゃない？！
Isn't that a donkey?!

125
00:13:21,016 --> 00:13:23,516
「ひーひー」？それ別のやつじゃん！
"Hee-hee"? That's a completely different one!

126
00:13:23,516 --> 00:13:26,516
ひーほー、ひーほー！
Hee-haw, hee-haw!

127
00:13:26,516 --> 00:13:29,016
オッケー、オッケー。「ひーふー、ひーふー」ね。
Okay, okay. "Hee-hoo, hee-hoo", right?

128
00:13:29,516 --> 00:13:31,016
じゃあ、続いてジジ！
Alright, next up, Gigi!

129
00:13:31,016 --> 00:13:34,016
えー...
Um...

130
00:13:35,016 --> 00:13:36,516
それ？！
That?!

131
00:13:38,816 --> 00:13:39,816
Wild horse!

132
00:13:39,816 --> 00:13:42,516
リアル！
So realistic!

133
00:13:43,016 --> 00:13:45,816
じゃあ、続いてべーちゃん！
Alright, next up, Bae-chan!

134
00:13:46,516 --> 00:13:51,016
えっと...「うまーーー！」
Um... "UMAAA---!"

135
00:13:51,016 --> 00:13:54,016
めっちゃ日本語しゃべるやん！
It speaks fluent Japanese!

136
00:13:56,516 --> 00:13:59,016
じゃあ、続いて、えー、ラオラ！
Alright, next up, Raora!

137
00:14:00,016 --> 00:14:04,516
Okay, maybe something like...

138
00:14:08,516 --> 00:14:10,516
すごーい！
Amazing!

139
00:14:10,516 --> 00:14:13,016
You're turning into a horse!

140
00:14:13,016 --> 00:14:14,016
リアル！
Realistic!

141
00:14:14,016 --> 00:14:15,516
You're a cat!

142
00:14:15,516 --> 00:14:17,516
めっちゃ似てた！
That was so spot on!

143
00:14:18,016 --> 00:14:21,016
じゃあ...
Alright...

144
00:14:22,016 --> 00:14:24,016
正解は...
The answer is...

145
00:14:24,016 --> 00:14:26,016
馬の鳴き声って何？
What is a horse sound?

146
00:14:26,016 --> 00:14:28,016
「ヒヒーン」でした！
It was "Hihiin"!

147
00:14:28,016 --> 00:14:29,016
ヒヒー？
Hi-hii?

148
00:14:28,816 --> 00:14:30,016
ヒヒーン？
Hihiin?

149
00:14:30,016 --> 00:14:32,016
ヒヒーン！Yes, yes, yes!
Hihiin! Yes, yes, yes!

150
00:14:32,016 --> 00:14:34,516
「ヒヒーン」！そしたらラオラじゃないの？
"Hihiin"! If so, isn't it Raora?

151
00:14:35,016 --> 00:14:38,016
ラオラはリアルすぎたかな？
Was Raora too realistic?

152
00:14:39,816 --> 00:14:41,516
リアルすぎたかな？
Maybe too realistic?

153
00:14:41,516 --> 00:14:43,016
ラオラ？
Raora?

154
00:14:43,016 --> 00:14:45,016
「ヒヒーン」？
ヒヒーン、うん。
"Hihiin"?
Hihiin, yeah.

155
00:14:44,816 --> 00:14:47,016
Oh, there's an "n" at the end!

156
00:14:47,016 --> 00:14:49,516
ヒ・ヒ・ー・ン。
ヒヒーン。
Hi-hi-i-n.
Hihiin.

157
00:14:49,816 --> 00:14:52,016
Why do horses make that sound?!

158
00:14:52,016 --> 00:14:54,016
Sounds like Michael Jackson!

159
00:14:54,016 --> 00:14:56,516
ヒヒーン！
Hihiin!

160
00:14:56,016 --> 00:14:58,516
ヒヒー！
Hee-hee!

161
00:15:00,024 --> 00:15:01,324
Kobo has "hihu" too.
Kobo wrote "hihu" too.

162
00:15:01,324 --> 00:15:03,024
Does it... am I count?
Does it... do I count?

163
00:15:03,024 --> 00:15:05,024
Oh yeah, Kobo does.

164
00:15:05,024 --> 00:15:07,524
Ah, hihu. I have "hihu" too.

165
00:15:07,524 --> 00:15:09,324
No, no hihu?

166
00:15:09,324 --> 00:15:11,024
No, "hihu" no.
No, no "hihu".

167
00:15:11,024 --> 00:15:12,324
フーの？
A "hoo"?

